REALROM sample.note e141 [NesBankingAnalyzer] Bank value is RESTORED here, not resolved: this call re-commits the bank READ BACK at e13f from write-through bank shadow 0021 -- a RAM cell the switch code keeps in step with every bank it commits, so the byte read is the last bank committed through it -- the save/restore idiom. The bank after this call is whatever 0021 held at that read, not a fresh value this analyzer failed to pin down. A property of the game, not a gap in analysis.
